/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Revelation chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("revelation", [
{n:1, name:"Alpha and Omega", seal:{ref:"Revelation 1:18",verse:"I am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore, Amen; and have the keys of hell and of death."}, facts:["Did you know Revelation is the only book of the Bible that opens with a blessing on the one who reads it aloud, and on those who hear and keep its words (Revelation 1:3)?","Did you know John received this Revelation on Patmos, a small rocky island where Rome had exiled him for preaching the word of God (Revelation 1:9)?","Did you know the seven stars are the angels of the seven churches, and the seven golden candlesticks are the seven churches themselves (Revelation 1:20)?"], questions:[
{q:"To whom was the Revelation given to be shown?", options:["His servants","Only the priests of Jerusalem","The kings of Asia","The angels alone"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:1",verse:"The Revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave unto him, to shew unto his servants things which must shortly come to pass; and he sent and signified it by his angel unto his servant John:", insight:"Revelation is not a puzzle for experts but a showing to servants; God wants His people to understand what must come."},
{q:"Of what three things did John bear record?", options:["The word of God, the testimony of Jesus Christ, and all things that he saw","Visions, dreams, and wonders of Rome","The law, the prophets, and the psalms","Signs, wonders, and miracles only"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:2",verse:"Who bare record of the word of God, and of the testimony of Jesus Christ, and of all things that he saw.", insight:"A faithful witness reports what he heard, what Christ testified, and what he saw; John held back nothing."},
{q:"Who does the opening blessing call blessed?", options:["He that reads, they that hear, and they that keep the words of this prophecy","Only those who preach it","Only those who can explain it","Only the seven churches"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:3",verse:"Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein: for the time is at hand.", insight:"The blessing rests on reading, hearing, and keeping; prophecy blesses the obedient, not the curious."},
{q:"Why does the blessing say the time is at hand?", options:["Because the time is at hand","Because the churches were old","Because John was dying","Because Rome was falling"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:3",verse:"Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein: for the time is at hand.", insight:"Nearness makes obedience urgent; when the time is at hand, keeping the word cannot wait."},
{q:"To whom does John address this letter?", options:["The seven churches which are in Asia","All the churches of Rome","The apostles at Jerusalem","The twelve tribes of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:4",verse:"John to the seven churches which are in Asia: Grace be unto you, and peace, from him which is, and which was, and which is to come; and from the seven Spirits which are before his throne;", insight:"God speaks to His churches by name and place; this letter is addressed, not general."},
{q:"From whom do grace and peace come in John's greeting?", options:["Him which is, and which was, and which is to come, and the seven Spirits before His throne","Moses and the prophets","The seven elders of Ephesus","The angels of the seven churches"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:4",verse:"John to the seven churches which are in Asia: Grace be unto you, and peace, from him which is, and which was, and which is to come; and from the seven Spirits which are before his throne;", insight:"Grace and peace flow from the eternal God and His perfect Spirit; no church stands on any other supply."},
{q:"What three titles does John give Jesus Christ?", options:["The faithful witness, the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth","The great teacher, the kind healer, and the humble servant","The lamb, the lion, and the morning star","The prophet, the priest, and the apostle"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:5",verse:"And from Jesus Christ, who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth. Unto him that loved us, and washed us from our sins in his own blood,", insight:"Faithful in witness, first in resurrection, prince over kings; Christ holds all three at once."},
{q:"What did Christ do for us in His own blood?", options:["Washed us from our sins","Paid our money debts","Gave us crowns of gold","Built us a temple"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:5",verse:"And from Jesus Christ, who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth. Unto him that loved us, and washed us from our sins in his own blood,", insight:"Cleansing comes by blood, not by effort; He did the washing, and we receive it."},
{q:"What has Christ made us unto God and His Father?", options:["Kings and priests","Servants and soldiers","Prophets and scribes","Judges and rulers"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:6",verse:"And hath made us kings and priests unto God and his Father; to him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.", insight:"Royalty and priesthood are given together; belonging to Christ both ennobles and consecrates you."},
{q:"How will Christ come, according to John?", options:["With clouds, and every eye shall see Him","Secretly to one city only","Only in dreams and visions","Silently, seen by no one"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:7",verse:"Behold, he cometh with clouds; and every eye shall see him, and they also which pierced him: and all kindreds of the earth shall wail because of him. Even so, Amen.", insight:"His coming will be visible to all, even to those who pierced Him; no one will miss it."},
{q:"What does the Lord call Himself?", options:["Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending","The first and the final prophet","The highest of the angels","The king of the islands"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:8",verse:"I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending, saith the Lord, which is, and which was, and which is to come, the Almighty.", insight:"He is the first letter and the last; every story begins and ends in Him."},
{q:"On what island was John when he received the Revelation?", options:["Patmos","Cyprus","Crete","Malta"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:9",verse:"I John, who also am your brother, and companion in tribulation, and in the kingdom and patience of Jesus Christ, was in the isle that is called Patmos, for the word of God, and for the testimony of Jesus Christ.", insight:"God gave the greatest unveiling on a prison island; confinement cannot confine Him."},
{q:"Why was John on the isle of Patmos?", options:["For the word of God, and for the testimony of Jesus Christ","For a crime against Rome","For fleeing his enemies","For a trading voyage"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:9",verse:"I John, who also am your brother, and companion in tribulation, and in the kingdom and patience of Jesus Christ, was in the isle that is called Patmos, for the word of God, and for the testimony of Jesus Christ.", insight:"He was not exiled for wrongdoing but for the word; suffering for Christ is a place of honor."},
{q:"On what day was John in the Spirit?", options:["The Lord's day","The Sabbath of rest","The feast of trumpets","The first day of the year"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:10",verse:"I was in the Spirit on the Lord’s day, and heard behind me a great voice, as of a trumpet,", insight:"Set apart to God even in exile, John kept the Lord's day, and the Lord met him in it."},
{q:"What was John commanded to do with what he saw?", options:["Write it in a book, and send it unto the seven churches","Tell it only to the elders","Hide it until the end","Sing it to the angels"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:11",verse:"Saying, I am Alpha and Omega, the first and the last: and, What thou seest, write in a book, and send it unto the seven churches which are in Asia; unto Ephesus, and unto Smyrna, and unto Pergamos, and unto Thyatira, and unto Sardis, and unto Philadelphia, and unto Laodicea.", insight:"Visions are meant to be written and sent; God intends His word to travel to His people."},
{q:"Who stood in the midst of the seven golden candlesticks?", options:["One like unto the Son of man","A great golden altar","An angel with a trumpet","A mighty cherub"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:13",verse:"And in the midst of the seven candlesticks one like unto the Son of man, clothed with a garment down to the foot, and girt about the paps with a golden girdle.", insight:"Christ stands in the middle of His churches; He is never distant from His own."},
{q:"How are Christ's head and hairs described?", options:["White like wool, as white as snow","Dark as the raven","Golden like the sun","Gray with age"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:14",verse:"His head and his hairs were white like wool, as white as snow; and his eyes were as a flame of fire;", insight:"White speaks of purity and eternal age; His holiness has no shadow in it."},
{q:"What is Christ's voice like?", options:["As the sound of many waters","As a whisper in the wind","As thunder without rain","As a still small voice"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:15",verse:"And his feet like unto fine brass, as if they burned in a furnace; and his voice as the sound of many waters.", insight:"Many waters carry both power and fullness; His voice drowns out every lesser noise."},
{q:"What did John do when he saw the glorified Christ?", options:["He fell at His feet as dead","He ran from the place","He laughed with joy","He closed his eyes"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:17",verse:"And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not; I am the first and the last:", insight:"Glory unmakes us before it remakes us; falling as dead is the honest first response."},
{q:"What do the seven stars and the seven candlesticks represent?", options:["The stars are the angels of the seven churches, and the candlesticks are the seven churches","The stars are the apostles, and the candlesticks are the elders","The stars are the prophets, and the candlesticks are the nations","The stars are the thrones, and the candlesticks are the crowns"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 1:20",verse:"The mystery of the seven stars which thou sawest in my right hand, and the seven golden candlesticks. The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches: and the seven candlesticks which thou sawest are the seven churches.", insight:"Heaven's symbols have heaven's meanings; Christ Himself unlocks the mystery for His churches."}
]},
{n:2, name:"The First Four Churches", seal:{ref:"Revelation 2:10",verse:"Fear none of those things which thou shalt suffer: behold, the devil shall cast some of you into prison, that ye may be tried; and ye shall have tribulation ten days: be thou faithful unto death, and I will give thee a crown of life."}, facts:["Did you know Pergamos is called the place where Satan's seat is, a city dominated by emperor worship and a great altar to Zeus that pressured Christians to deny Christ (Revelation 2:13)?","Did you know Christ called the poor Christians of Smyrna rich, measuring wealth by heaven's ledger and not by Rome's (Revelation 2:9)?","Did you know a white stone was used in the ancient world as a token of acquittal or welcome, which makes the overcomer's white stone a mark of God's own approval (Revelation 2:17)?"], questions:[
{q:"How does Christ introduce Himself to the church of Ephesus?", options:["As He that holds the seven stars in His right hand and walks in the midst of the seven golden candlesticks","As the lion of the tribe of Judah","As the bright and morning star","As the Amen, the faithful witness"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:1",verse:"Unto the angel of the church of Ephesus write; These things saith he that holdeth the seven stars in his right hand, who walketh in the midst of the seven golden candlesticks;", insight:"He comes holding and walking among them; Christ is near enough to see and strong enough to keep."},
{q:"What did Ephesus do to those who claimed to be apostles?", options:["Tried them, found them liars","Welcomed them as teachers","Paid them with silver","Sent them to Rome"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:2",verse:"I know thy works, and thy labour, and thy patience, and how thou canst not bear them which are evil: and thou hast tried them which say they are apostles, and are not, and hast found them liars:", insight:"Ephesus tested claims instead of swallowing them; discernment guards the church from flattery."},
{q:"What does Christ commend about Ephesus's labour?", options:["They bore, had patience, laboured for His name's sake, and had not fainted","They built a great temple","They converted the governor","They wrote many letters"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:3",verse:"And hast borne, and hast patience, and for my name’s sake hast laboured, and hast not fainted.", insight:"Steadfast labour for His name is precious to Christ, even when the heart has cooled."},
{q:"What did Christ have against Ephesus?", options:["They had left their first love","They had denied His name","They had worshipped idols","They had stopped giving"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:4",verse:"Nevertheless I have somewhat against thee, because thou hast left thy first love.", insight:"You can keep the works and lose the love; Christ wants the heart, not only the hands."},
{q:"What would happen to Ephesus's candlestick if they did not repent?", options:["Christ would remove it out of its place","It would be carried to Rome","It would be given to Smyrna","It would shine brighter than ever"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:5",verse:"Remember therefore from whence thou art fallen, and repent, and do the first works; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will remove thy candlestick out of his place, except thou repent.", insight:"A church that will not repent can lose its light; presence among the candlesticks is not permanent."},
{q:"What did Ephesus hate, which Christ also hated?", options:["The deeds of the Nicolaitanes","The songs of the temple","The letters of Paul","The markets of the city"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:6",verse:"But this thou hast, that thou hatest the deeds of the Nicolaitanes, which I also hate.", insight:"Hating what Christ hates is part of loving Him; some things deserve the church's hatred."},
{q:"What is promised to the overcomer in Ephesus?", options:["To eat of the tree of life in the midst of the paradise of God","A crown of pure gold","A throne beside the elders","The key of David"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:7",verse:"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of God.", insight:"The tree of life lost in Eden is given back in paradise; overcoming restores what sin forfeited."},
{q:"How does Christ introduce Himself to the church in Smyrna?", options:["The first and the last, which was dead, and is alive","The Son of God with eyes of fire","He that hath the key of David","The Amen, the true witness"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:8",verse:"And unto the angel of the church in Smyrna write; These things saith the first and the last, which was dead, and is alive;", insight:"To a church facing death, He comes as the One who died and lives; His resurrection is their courage."},
{q:"What did Christ say about Smyrna's poverty?", options:["They were in poverty, but were rich","They were poor and forgotten","They were rich in silver","They had lost all they owned"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:9",verse:"I know thy works, and tribulation, and poverty, (but thou art rich) and I know the blasphemy of them which say they are Jews, and are not, but are the synagogue of Satan.", insight:"Heaven's riches do not show in a ledger; the poorest church can be the richest."},
{q:"How long would Smyrna's tribulation last?", options:["Ten days","Forty years","Seven months","One night"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:10",verse:"Fear none of those things which thou shalt suffer: behold, the devil shall cast some of you into prison, that ye may be tried; and ye shall have tribulation ten days: be thou faithful unto death, and I will give thee a crown of life.", insight:"Bounded trials are bearable; Christ sets the limit before He allows the testing."},
{q:"What promise is given to the one faithful unto death?", options:["A crown of life","A white stone","The morning star","Hidden manna"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:10",verse:"Fear none of those things which thou shalt suffer: behold, the devil shall cast some of you into prison, that ye may be tried; and ye shall have tribulation ten days: be thou faithful unto death, and I will give thee a crown of life.", insight:"Faithfulness to the end wears a crown; death is not the end of the faithful."},
{q:"What shall the overcomer not be hurt of?", options:["The second death","The first famine","The night watches","The winter cold"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:11",verse:"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; He that overcometh shall not be hurt of the second death.", insight:"The second death has no claim on the overcomer; one death conquered ends death's power."},
{q:"Where did the church in Pergamos dwell?", options:["Where Satan's seat is","In the wilderness of Judea","Beside the river Euphrates","On the island of Patmos"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:13",verse:"I know thy works, and where thou dwellest, even where Satan’s seat is: and thou holdest fast my name, and hast not denied my faith, even in those days wherein Antipas was my faithful martyr, who was slain among you, where Satan dwelleth.", insight:"Faithfulness in the hardest place shines brightest; Pergamos held fast where evil sat enthroned."},
{q:"Who was slain as Christ's faithful martyr at Pergamos?", options:["Antipas","Polycarp","Stephen","James"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:13",verse:"I know thy works, and where thou dwellest, even where Satan’s seat is: and thou holdest fast my name, and hast not denied my faith, even in those days wherein Antipas was my faithful martyr, who was slain among you, where Satan dwelleth.", insight:"Christ names His martyr and remembers where he fell; heaven keeps the record of earth's faithful."},
{q:"What was the doctrine of Balaam that troubled Pergamos?", options:["Teaching to eat things sacrificed unto idols and to commit fornication","Teaching that Christ never died","Teaching that prayer is useless","Teaching that the law is ended"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:14",verse:"But I have a few things against thee, because thou hast there them that hold the doctrine of Balaam, who taught Balac to cast a stumblingblock before the children of Israel, to eat things sacrificed unto idols, and to commit fornication.", insight:"Balaam could not curse Israel, so he corrupted her; the church's danger is compromise, not curses."},
{q:"What three gifts are promised to the overcomer in Pergamos?", options:["Hidden manna, a white stone, and a new name","Gold, silver, and precious stones","A sword, a shield, and a crown","Wine, oil, and bread"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:17",verse:"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the hidden manna, and will give him a white stone, and in the stone a new name written, which no man knoweth saving he that receiveth it.", insight:"Secret bread, a personal stone, a known name; heaven's rewards are intimate, not public."},
{q:"How does Christ appear to the church in Thyatira?", options:["With eyes like unto a flame of fire, and feet like fine brass","With hair white as snow and a golden crown","With a sickle in His hand","With a rainbow about His head"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:18",verse:"And unto the angel of the church in Thyatira write; These things saith the Son of God, who hath his eyes like unto a flame of fire, and his feet are like fine brass;", insight:"Eyes of fire see through pretense; feet of brass will tread the false down. He sees and He judges."},
{q:"What did Christ condemn in Thyatira?", options:["Suffering the woman Jezebel, who called herself a prophetess, to teach and seduce His servants","Building a temple to idols","Denying His name before rulers","Refusing to give to the poor"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:20",verse:"Notwithstanding I have a few things against thee, because thou sufferest that woman Jezebel, which calleth herself a prophetess, to teach and to seduce my servants to commit fornication, and to eat things sacrificed unto idols.", insight:"Tolerance of false teaching is not love; letting Jezebel teach poisons the servants Christ loves."},
{q:"What had Christ given Jezebel, which she refused?", options:["Space to repent of her fornication","Gold and silver","A throne in the church","Power over nations"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:21",verse:"And I gave her space to repent of her fornication; and she repented not.", insight:"God gives room to repent before He judges; refusing the space leaves only the sentence."},
{q:"What authority is promised to the overcomer in Thyatira?", options:["Power over the nations, to rule them with a rod of iron","Power to forgive sins","Power over the winds","Power to open the seals"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 2:27",verse:"And he shall rule them with a rod of iron; as the vessels of a potter shall they be broken to shivers: even as I received of my Father.", insight:"Those who endure under Christ will reign with Him; present patience becomes future authority."}
]},
{n:3, name:"The Last Three Churches", seal:{ref:"Revelation 3:20",verse:"Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me."}, facts:["Did you know Laodicea was a wealthy banking and textile city famous for its eye salve, so Christ's counsel to buy eyesalve and His charge of blindness carried a local sting (Revelation 3:18)?","Did you know Sardis had a name that it was alive, but Christ said it was dead, a church with a reputation but no real life (Revelation 3:1)?","Did you know Philadelphia had only a little strength, yet Christ set before her an open door no man can shut, showing open doors are kept by faithfulness, not power (Revelation 3:8)?"], questions:[
{q:"How does Christ introduce Himself to the church in Sardis?", options:["He that hath the seven Spirits of God, and the seven stars","The first and the last","The Son of God","The lion of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:1",verse:"And unto the angel of the church in Sardis write; These things saith he that hath the seven Spirits of God, and the seven stars; I know thy works, that thou hast a name that thou livest, and art dead.", insight:"He comes with the fullness of the Spirit and the churches in His hand; nothing in Sardis escapes His notice."},
{q:"What was Sardis's deadly condition?", options:["They had a name that they lived, and were dead","They had denied the faith","They had burned the Scriptures","They had fled the city"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:1",verse:"And unto the angel of the church in Sardis write; These things saith he that hath the seven Spirits of God, and the seven stars; I know thy works, that thou hast a name that thou livest, and art dead.", insight:"A living name can cover a dead heart; reputation is not life, and Christ knows the difference."},
{q:"What does Christ command the dying church in Sardis?", options:["Be watchful, and strengthen the things which remain, that are ready to die","Close the doors and flee","Build a higher wall","Choose a new pastor"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:2",verse:"Be watchful, and strengthen the things which remain, that are ready to die: for I have not found thy works perfect before God.", insight:"Strengthen what remains; God works with remnants, and small embers can be fanned to flame."},
{q:"How will Christ come upon the unwatchful in Sardis?", options:["As a thief, at an hour they will not know","As a friend at noon","As a king with trumpets","As a shepherd at dawn"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:3",verse:"Remember therefore how thou hast received and heard, and hold fast, and repent. If therefore thou shalt not watch, I will come on thee as a thief, and thou shalt not know what hour I will come upon thee.", insight:"The unwatchful are surprised; watching is the church's duty, not an option."},
{q:"Who in Sardis had not defiled their garments?", options:["A few names who would walk with Christ in white","The seven elders","The children only","The rich merchants"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:4",verse:"Thou hast a few names even in Sardis which have not defiled their garments; and they shall walk with me in white: for they are worthy.", insight:"Even in a dying church, a faithful few keep their garments clean; God always has His remnant."},
{q:"What is promised to the overcomer in Sardis?", options:["White raiment, and his name kept in the book of life","A crown of iron","A seat in Rome","Silver and gold"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:5",verse:"He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.", insight:"White garments for a clean walk, a kept name for a kept faith; heaven remembers its own."},
{q:"What will Christ do with the overcomer's name?", options:["Confess it before His Father, and before His angels","Write it in the sand","Hide it from the churches","Seal it in a book unseen"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:5",verse:"He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.", insight:"Christ will speak your name before the Father; be faithful on earth and He will own you in heaven."},
{q:"How does Christ introduce Himself to Philadelphia?", options:["He that is holy, he that is true, he that hath the key of David","The Alpha and Omega","The bright morning star","The root of Jesse"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:7",verse:"And to the angel of the church in Philadelphia write; These things saith he that is holy, he that is true, he that hath the key of David, he that openeth, and no man shutteth; and shutteth, and no man openeth;", insight:"Holy, true, and holding David's key; His authority opens what no man can shut."},
{q:"What had Philadelphia done with her little strength?", options:["Kept His word, and had not denied His name","Built a great cathedral","Conquered the nations","Written many books"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:8",verse:"I know thy works: behold, I have set before thee an open door, and no man can shut it: for thou hast a little strength, and hast kept my word, and hast not denied my name.", insight:"Little strength with kept word outweighs great strength with compromise; faithfulness opens doors."},
{q:"What will happen to those of the synagogue of Satan who opposed Philadelphia?", options:["They will come and worship before her feet, and know that Christ has loved her","They will be crowned with gold","They will rule the city","They will be forgotten"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:9",verse:"Behold, I will make them of the synagogue of Satan, which say they are Jews, and are not, but do lie; behold, I will make them to come and worship before thy feet, and to know that I have loved thee.", insight:"God vindicates the faithful in the sight of their accusers; love proven will be seen."},
{q:"From what would the faithful in Philadelphia be kept?", options:["The hour of temptation which shall come upon all the world","The winter famine","The Roman tax","The plague of locusts"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:10",verse:"Because thou hast kept the word of my patience, I also will keep thee from the hour of temptation, which shall come upon all the world, to try them that dwell upon the earth.", insight:"Kept patience brings kept protection; those who guard His word are guarded in trial."},
{q:"What warning protects Philadelphia's crown?", options:["Hold fast what thou hast, that no man take thy crown","Hide thy crown in the earth","Give thy crown to the elders","Sell thy crown for bread"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:11",verse:"Behold, I come quickly: hold that fast which thou hast, that no man take thy crown.", insight:"Crowns can be lost by letting go; holding fast is the whole of perseverance."},
{q:"What three names will be written upon the overcomer in Philadelphia?", options:["The name of His God, the name of the new Jerusalem, and His new name","The names of the twelve apostles","The names of the seven churches","The names of Moses, Elijah, and David"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:12",verse:"Him that overcometh will I make a pillar in the temple of my God, and he shall go no more out: and I will write upon him the name of my God, and the name of the city of my God, which is new Jerusalem, which cometh down out of heaven from my God: and I will write upon him my new name.", insight:"God writes His own name on His own; the overcomer becomes a living pillar in His temple."},
{q:"How does Christ introduce Himself to the Laodiceans?", options:["The Amen, the faithful and true witness, the beginning of the creation of God","The lamb that was slain","The king of the Jews","The good shepherd"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:14",verse:"And unto the angel of the church of the Laodiceans write; These things saith the Amen, the faithful and true witness, the beginning of the creation of God;", insight:"The Amen, the faithful witness, speaks to the unfaithful; truth itself addresses their lukewarmness."},
{q:"How did Christ describe Laodicea's works?", options:["Neither cold nor hot","Burning with zeal","Frozen in fear","Boiling with anger"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:15",verse:"I know thy works, that thou art neither cold nor hot: I would thou wert cold or hot.", insight:"Lukewarm is its own verdict; Christ would rather have cold or hot than comfortable."},
{q:"What will Christ do with the lukewarm church?", options:["Spue them out of His mouth","Cast them into the sea","Burn them with fire","Leave them in peace"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:16",verse:"So then because thou art lukewarm, and neither cold nor hot, I will spue thee out of my mouth.", insight:"Lukewarmness sickens the Lord; comfort that needs nothing is the most dangerous condition."},
{q:"What did Laodicea say about herself, and what was she really?", options:["She said she was rich and had need of nothing, but was wretched, miserable, poor, blind, and naked","She said she was poor, but was rich","She said she was blind, but could see","She said she was naked, but was clothed"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:17",verse:"Because thou sayest, I am rich, and increased with goods, and have need of nothing; and knowest not that thou art wretched, and miserable, and poor, and blind, and naked:", insight:"Self-sufficiency blinds; the church that needs nothing cannot see its own nakedness."},
{q:"What three things does Christ counsel Laodicea to buy from Him?", options:["Gold tried in the fire, white raiment, and eyesalve","Wheat, wine, and oil","Silver, brass, and iron","Houses, lands, and ships"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:18",verse:"I counsel thee to buy of me gold tried in the fire, that thou mayest be rich; and white raiment, that thou mayest be clothed, and that the shame of thy nakedness do not appear; and anoint thine eyes with eyesalve, that thou mayest see.", insight:"True riches, true covering, true sight are bought from Him alone; the market of heaven takes repentance as coin."},
{q:"What does Christ say about His rebukes?", options:["As many as He loves, He rebukes and chastens","He never rebukes His own","He rebukes only strangers","His rebukes are without love"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:19",verse:"As many as I love, I rebuke and chasten: be zealous therefore, and repent.", insight:"Rebuke is a mark of love, not anger; chastening proves you are His."},
{q:"What promise does Christ make to the one who opens the door?", options:["He will come in and sup with him, and he with Him","He will give him a crown at once","He will make him a ruler","He will take him to heaven"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 3:20",verse:"Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.", insight:"He knocks and waits; the opened door becomes a table, and the guest becomes a friend."}
]},
{n:4, name:"The Throne in Heaven", seal:{ref:"Revelation 4:11",verse:"Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honour and power: for thou hast created all things, and for thy pleasure they are and were created."}, facts:["Did you know the four living creatures, like a lion, a calf, a man, and a flying eagle, echo the cherubim of Ezekiel's vision, showing heaven's worship has one unchanging pattern (Revelation 4:7)?","Did you know the twenty-four elders casting their crowns before the throne is worship's truest picture, every honor laid back at the feet of the One who gave it (Revelation 4:10)?","Did you know the sea of glass like crystal pictures the calm, pure holiness before God's throne, a stillness no storm can reach (Revelation 4:6)?"], questions:[
{q:"How is He that sat on the throne described when the beasts give Him glory?", options:["Who liveth for ever and ever","Who was slain for the world","Who holds the seven stars","Who walks in the garden"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:9",verse:"And when those beasts give glory and honour and thanks to him that sat on the throne, who liveth for ever and ever,", insight:"He liveth for ever and ever; the throne endures because its King never ends."},
{q:"What did the trumpet-like voice say to John?", options:["Come up hither","Go down to the sea","Return to Patmos","Write no more"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:1",verse:"After this I looked, and, behold, a door was opened in heaven: and the first voice which I heard was as it were of a trumpet talking with me; which said, Come up hither, and I will shew thee things which must be hereafter.", insight:"'Come up hither' is God's invitation to higher sight; heaven's view changes earth's troubles."},
{q:"What would be shown to John?", options:["Things which must be hereafter","The history of Rome","The wealth of nations","The end of the sea"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:1",verse:"After this I looked, and, behold, a door was opened in heaven: and the first voice which I heard was as it were of a trumpet talking with me; which said, Come up hither, and I will shew thee things which must be hereafter.", insight:"Prophecy looks forward by God's showing, not by man's guessing; the future is revealed, not invented."},
{q:"In what state was John when he saw the throne?", options:["Immediately in the spirit","Asleep in a dream","Walking on the shore","Praying at the temple"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:2",verse:"And immediately I was in the spirit: and, behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat on the throne.", insight:"The Spirit lifts us to see what flesh cannot; heavenly vision needs a heavenly state."},
{q:"What was set in heaven, and who was there?", options:["A throne, and one sat on the throne","An altar, and a priest stood","A table, and elders ate","A gate, and angels watched"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:2",verse:"And immediately I was in the spirit: and, behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat on the throne.", insight:"All heaven centers on one seated figure; the universe has a throne, and it is occupied."},
{q:"What did He that sat on the throne look like?", options:["Like a jasper and a sardine stone","Like burning coal","Like a pillar of cloud","Like a man of war"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:3",verse:"And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone: and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like unto an emerald.", insight:"Jasper's clarity and sardius's deep red speak of purity and judgment; God's glory has many facets."},
{q:"What was round about the throne?", options:["A rainbow, in sight like unto an emerald","A wall of fire","A cloud of darkness","A river of light"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:3",verse:"And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone: and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like unto an emerald.", insight:"The rainbow remembers mercy in the midst of majesty; judgment sits, but promise surrounds it."},
{q:"How many elders sat on the seats around the throne?", options:["Four and twenty","Twelve","Seven","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:4",verse:"And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.", insight:"Twenty-four elders, the full number of God's people crowned and robed; heaven's council is complete."},
{q:"What were the elders clothed in, and what was on their heads?", options:["White raiment, and crowns of gold","Purple robes, and crowns of thorns","Sackcloth, and ashes","Armor, and helmets of brass"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:4",verse:"And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.", insight:"White for righteousness, gold for royalty; the redeemed wear both in His presence."},
{q:"What proceeded out of the throne?", options:["Lightnings and thunderings and voices","Smoke and darkness","Wind and hail","Fire and brimstone"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:5",verse:"And out of the throne proceeded lightnings and thunderings and voices: and there were seven lamps of fire burning before the throne, which are the seven Spirits of God.", insight:"God's throne speaks in power; His majesty is not silent but thunders."},
{q:"What burned before the throne?", options:["Seven lamps of fire, which are the seven Spirits of God","Seven golden bowls","Seven silver trumpets","Seven brazen altars"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:5",verse:"And out of the throne proceeded lightnings and thunderings and voices: and there were seven lamps of fire burning before the throne, which are the seven Spirits of God.", insight:"The Spirit burns complete before the throne; seven lamps, one perfect flame of God."},
{q:"What was before the throne?", options:["A sea of glass like unto crystal","A field of wheat","A mountain of brass","A garden of trees"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:6",verse:"And before the throne there was a sea of glass like unto crystal: and in the midst of the throne, and round about the throne, were four beasts full of eyes before and behind.", insight:"Crystal stillness before the throne; in God's presence there is no troubled water."},
{q:"What were the four beasts full of?", options:["Eyes before and behind","Wings of iron","Hands of brass","Feet of clay"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:6",verse:"And before the throne there was a sea of glass like unto crystal: and in the midst of the throne, and round about the throne, were four beasts full of eyes before and behind.", insight:"Full of eyes, they see all; heaven's servants miss nothing of God's glory."},
{q:"Which beast was like a flying eagle?", options:["The fourth beast","The first beast","The second beast","The third beast"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:7",verse:"And the first beast was like a lion, and the second beast like a calf, and the third beast had a face as a man, and the fourth beast was like a flying eagle.", insight:"Lion, calf, man, eagle; all creation's strength, service, reason, and swiftness worship at the throne."},
{q:"Which beast was like a calf?", options:["The second beast","The first beast","The third beast","The fourth beast"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:7",verse:"And the first beast was like a lion, and the second beast like a calf, and the third beast had a face as a man, and the fourth beast was like a flying eagle.", insight:"The calf speaks of patient service and sacrifice; even strength serves in heaven."},
{q:"How many wings did each of the four beasts have?", options:["Six","Two","Four","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:8",verse:"And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.", insight:"Six wings for swift obedience; heaven's servants are ready to fly at His word."},
{q:"What do the beasts say day and night without rest?", options:["Holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come","Glory to the highest heaven","Peace on earth forever","Worthy is the Lamb"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:8",verse:"And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.", insight:"Ceaseless holiness is heaven's song; rest is not needed where worship is delight."},
{q:"To whom do the beasts give glory and honour and thanks?", options:["Him that sat on the throne, who liveth for ever and ever","The twenty-four elders","The seven angels","The saints on earth"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:9",verse:"And when those beasts give glory and honour and thanks to him that sat on the throne, who liveth for ever and ever,", insight:"All glory flows upward to the eternal One; heaven's worship has one direction."},
{q:"What do the elders do with their crowns?", options:["Cast them before the throne","Polish them with care","Hide them in their robes","Give them to the beasts"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:10",verse:"The four and twenty elders fall down before him that sat on the throne, and worship him that liveth for ever and ever, and cast their crowns before the throne, saying,", insight:"The highest honor is to lay honor down; crowns are most glorious at His feet."},
{q:"Why is the Lord worthy to receive glory, honour, and power?", options:["For He has created all things, and for His pleasure they are and were created","For He has destroyed His enemies","For He has gathered much gold","For He has built the heavens alone"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 4:11",verse:"Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honour and power: for thou hast created all things, and for thy pleasure they are and were created.", insight:"Creation is the ground of worship; all things exist for His pleasure, and He is worthy."}
]},
{n:5, name:"The Lamb and the Sealed Book", seal:{ref:"Revelation 5:12",verse:"Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing."}, facts:["Did you know the golden vials full of odours are the prayers of saints, which means your prayers rise before God's throne like incense and are never wasted (Revelation 5:8)?","Did you know the Lamb who opens the seals still stands as though slain, showing heaven honors Christ's sacrifice forever (Revelation 5:6)?","Did you know the redeemed are gathered out of every kindred, tongue, people, and nation, the widest welcome ever sung (Revelation 5:9)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did John see in the right hand of Him that sat on the throne?", options:["A book written within and on the backside, sealed with seven seals","A sword of flame","A golden crown","A silver trumpet"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:1",verse:"And I saw in the right hand of him that sat on the throne a book written within and on the backside, sealed with seven seals.", insight:"The book holds God's purposes, written on both sides and sealed; His plans are full and secure."},
{q:"How many seals were on the book?", options:["Seven","Three","Twelve","Ten"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:1",verse:"And I saw in the right hand of him that sat on the throne a book written within and on the backside, sealed with seven seals.", insight:"Seven seals, complete and unbroken; only the worthy One may open what God has sealed."},
{q:"What did the strong angel proclaim with a loud voice?", options:["Who is worthy to open the book, and to loose the seals thereof","Who will build the temple","Who shall judge the nations","Who will sing the new song"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:2",verse:"And I saw a strong angel proclaiming with a loud voice, Who is worthy to open the book, and to loose the seals thereof?", insight:"Worthiness is the question heaven asks; the book waits for the right hands."},
{q:"Who was able to open the book?", options:["No man in heaven, nor in earth, neither under the earth","The twenty-four elders","The four beasts","The seven angels"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:3",verse:"And no man in heaven, nor in earth, neither under the earth, was able to open the book, neither to look thereon.", insight:"All creation searched, none found worthy; the need reveals how great the Worthy One must be."},
{q:"Why did John weep much?", options:["Because no man was found worthy to open and to read the book, neither to look thereon","Because the throne was empty","Because the elders had fallen","Because the book was burned"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:4",verse:"And I wept much, because no man was found worthy to open and to read the book, neither to look thereon.", insight:"John wept because a sealed book means a stalled purpose; his tears show how much God's plan matters."},
{q:"What did one of the elders say to the weeping John?", options:["Weep not","Fear not the angels","Be silent","Depart in peace"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:5",verse:"And one of the elders saith unto me, Weep not: behold, the Lion of the tribe of Juda, the Root of David, hath prevailed to open the book, and to loose the seven seals thereof.", insight:"'Weep not' comes with a reason; heaven's comfort always points to Christ."},
{q:"Who had prevailed to open the book?", options:["The Lion of the tribe of Juda, the Root of David","The prince of Persia","The king of Salem","The angel of the covenant"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:5",verse:"And one of the elders saith unto me, Weep not: behold, the Lion of the tribe of Juda, the Root of David, hath prevailed to open the book, and to loose the seven seals thereof.", insight:"Lion and Root, conqueror and source; Christ prevails because of who He is, not what He attempts."},
{q:"What stood in the midst of the throne and the elders?", options:["A Lamb as it had been slain","A golden altar","A great white throne","A pillar of fire"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:6",verse:"And I beheld, and, lo, in the midst of the throne and of the four beasts, and in the midst of the elders, stood a Lamb as it had been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of God sent forth into all the earth.", insight:"The Lion is a Lamb, and the Lamb bears wounds; heaven's conqueror conquered by being slain."},
{q:"How many horns and eyes did the Lamb have?", options:["Seven horns and seven eyes","Two horns and two eyes","Twelve horns and twelve eyes","One horn and one eye"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:6",verse:"And I beheld, and, lo, in the midst of the throne and of the four beasts, and in the midst of the elders, stood a Lamb as it had been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of God sent forth into all the earth.", insight:"Seven horns for perfect power, seven eyes for perfect sight; the Lamb lacks nothing."},
{q:"Whose voices join the praise of the Lamb in Revelation 5:13?", options:["Every creature in heaven, and on the earth, and under the earth, and in the sea","Only the four beasts","Only the twenty-four elders","The seven spirits alone"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:13",verse:"And every creature which is in heaven, and on the earth, and under the earth, and such as are in the sea, and all that are in them, heard I saying, Blessing, and honour, and glory, and power, be unto him that sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb for ever and ever.", insight:"Every creature joins the song; in the end, praise has no bystanders."},
{q:"What did the Lamb do with the book?", options:["He came and took it out of the right hand of Him that sat upon the throne","He cast it into the sea","He gave it to the elders","He hid it under the altar"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:7",verse:"And he came and took the book out of the right hand of him that sat upon the throne.", insight:"He took the book; the plan of God rests in the pierced hands that are worthy to unfold it."},
{q:"What did the beasts and elders do when the Lamb took the book?", options:["Fell down before the Lamb","Fled from the throne","Covered their faces","Sang to the angels"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:8",verse:"And when he had taken the book, the four beasts and four and twenty elders fell down before the Lamb, having every one of them harps, and golden vials full of odours, which are the prayers of saints.", insight:"Heaven falls down before the Lamb; the worthiest act of the worthiest beings is worship."},
{q:"What did every one of them hold?", options:["Harps, and golden vials full of odours","Swords and shields","Crowns and scepters","Books and scrolls"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:8",verse:"And when he had taken the book, the four beasts and four and twenty elders fell down before the Lamb, having every one of them harps, and golden vials full of odours, which are the prayers of saints.", insight:"Harps for praise and vials for prayer; heaven holds both music and intercession."},
{q:"What did the four beasts say to the Lamb's praise?", options:["Amen","Hallelujah","Holy, holy, holy","Worthy is the Lamb"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:14",verse:"And the four beasts said, Amen. And the four and twenty elders fell down and worshipped him that liveth for ever and ever.", insight:"The beasts answer with Amen; heaven seals its own worship with agreement."},
{q:"What did the new song declare the Lamb worthy to do?", options:["To take the book, and to open the seals thereof","To judge the living","To build the new temple","To gather the stars"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:9",verse:"And they sung a new song, saying, Thou art worthy to take the book, and to open the seals thereof: for thou wast slain, and hast redeemed us to God by thy blood out of every kindred, and tongue, and people, and nation;", insight:"New mercies deserve a new song; the Lamb's worth is heaven's newest and oldest theme."},
{q:"Why is the Lamb worthy?", options:["He was slain, and has redeemed us to God by His blood","He was born in Bethlehem","He taught the multitudes","He walked on the sea"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:9",verse:"And they sung a new song, saying, Thou art worthy to take the book, and to open the seals thereof: for thou wast slain, and hast redeemed us to God by thy blood out of every kindred, and tongue, and people, and nation;", insight:"Worthiness is measured in blood shed; redemption is the ground of all His honor."},
{q:"From whose right hand did the Lamb take the book?", options:["Him that sat upon the throne","The strong angel","One of the elders","The archangel Michael"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:7",verse:"And he came and took the book out of the right hand of him that sat upon the throne.", insight:"The book passes from the Father's hand to the Lamb's; redemption's plan moves from throne to Son."},
{q:"What has the Lamb made us, and what shall we do?", options:["Kings and priests unto our God, and we shall reign on the earth","Prophets and judges forever","Servants in the temple","Singers in the choir"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:10",verse:"And hast made us unto our God kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth.", insight:"Redeemed to reign; salvation lifts us from slavery to royalty under God."},
{q:"How many angels were round about the throne?", options:["Ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands","A hundred and forty-four thousand","Seven thousand","Twelve legions"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:11",verse:"And I beheld, and I heard the voice of many angels round about the throne and the beasts and the elders: and the number of them was ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands;", insight:"Myriads upon myriads; heaven's host is countless, and every voice joins the praise."},
{q:"What did the angels ascribe to the Lamb that was slain?", options:["Power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing","Gold, and silver, and jewels","Kingdoms, and thrones, and crowns","Songs, and harps, and trumpets"], a:0, ref:"Revelation 5:12",verse:"Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.", insight:"Sevenfold praise for the seven-sealed book's Opener; the Lamb receives all, for He gave all."}
]}
]);
